    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_77 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Xavier explains Burrow architecture" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "I mean, yeah, that sounds rad. My slack alternative is called Burrow. The thesis is that AI is moving to the edges, so we should do AI on the edge rather than on the center. And that means that every device does its own transcription. So the conversation we're having is part of the, like, timeline. And the video frames of, like, your screen sharing becomes part of the timeline. It gets OCR'd in the timeline. And so similar, like this, Zoom is no longer a memory hole the same way it used to be, because right now, Zoom's in memory hall." ;
                oa:prefix "t to see?\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** Totally. I m" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "12418"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "12958"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_78 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Tanya explains aswritten AI pilot and provenance" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Totally. I mean, we may have some similar thoughts in the middle. Basically, what. What I've seen is that most organizations are constantly rehashing the same conversations over and over again. You end up on a Zoom call and, you know, like my pilot client, they run engineering governance over Zoom, right? As everyone does. Like, they have cadence meetings, they have standups, and they also have, like, daily meeting where product owners come in and ask the chief architect all sorts of stuff, right? They say, oh, like, can we do it this way for this particular client and how long would it take us to fix this thing? And, you know, an engineer comes in and says, hey, I wrote this spec. Does this look good to you? Right? And this meeting is actually the source of truth for how things are done at the company, right? And yet nobody writes it down like There is a transcript, but those things aren't actually usable or actionable at all. And so the first thing that I created for them was the ability to ingest all of those calls and then give all of these product owners and engineers an MCP server that whenever they start their session and they say, hey, want to spec this feature? Or I'm talking to this client about whatever, it pulls in all of the conversation data and then cites the ideas and actual conversations by name and date in the responses to the person. Right. So you get full provenance of the ideas and you can essentially tell whether an AI is hallucinated or not by whether or not it cited someone that actually said it." ;
                oa:prefix "memory hall.\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** Correct. " ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "12976"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "14521"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_79 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Provenance and truth in transcripts" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Correct. Exactly. And the transcript is the truth, because it exists." ;
                oa:prefix " said it.\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** The transcri" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "14542"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "14611"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_80 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Graph scaling and perspective querying" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "The transcript is the truth. But then from there the perspective becomes a way to interrogate the truth and it changes over time. So if I ask why are we applying to OIC and what has influenced the decision over time, it calls as written and reads from the perspective and expands the graph. And it took a while to figure out how to make this so that it doesn't exponentially scale. Right? Because after a while these graph reads get absolutely fucking massive. And when it's small, you can just dump the entire graph into the LLM context and it works great, but you can't. It gets way bigger really fast." ;
                oa:prefix "e it exists.\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** Yes, exac" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "14629"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "15233"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_81 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Graph scaling and perspective querying" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Yes, exactly. That's been the core problem with linkwell Undertow is like all of the knowledge graph tools dump the entire graph into the prompt and use that as the way it builds the future graph nodes. And that just doesn't work." ;
                oa:prefix "lly fast.\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** Well, I solv" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "15254"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "15484"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_82 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "V2 ontology, graph collapse, provenance, permissioning" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Well, I solved that. And it's honestly rather complicated. We could have an entire conversation Talking about the V2 Ontology and how I did collapse and expand around graphs and this digest narration and how that is able to have full provenance inside of digested nodes. And like, how that can also support security where you can have permissioning, where, like an actor can only see the calls that they actually attended, but you can still have this summarized node that has like that stuff inside of it. Right? Like." ;
                oa:prefix "oesn't work.\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** Yes, beca" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "15502"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "16020"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_83 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Knowledge anchors and fact provenance in Iceland project" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Yes, because each. Yeah, exactly, each. This is the thing I'm doing for Iceland. Like, every single claim has a like anchor to it. That anchor is associated with, like, research. That claim may not actually show up in the text ad that like, gets deployed, but it may be part of what isn't the inference that built that. So every single fact has attributes and knowledge anchors associated with it. And then that fact is part of a timeline. It can be superseded. It has relationships with people." ;
                oa:prefix "ht? Like.\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** Yep. Yeah. E" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "16041"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "16536"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_84 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Storage architecture and zero data retention" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Yep. Yeah. Exactly. And so what's interesting about this is the entire graph is append only it lives in your GitHub repo. So I don't store any data, which is kind of wild. I actually operate entirely as the Zero data retention processor, which is cool. So it can be deployed on prem. It can be deployed completely enterprise safe. But yeah, when you ask things you get an AI response, but it can give you citations." ;
                oa:prefix "with people.\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** You shoul" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "16554"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "16969"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

