    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_100 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "question" ;
        narr:context "Tanya's fundraising, pricing, and enterprise pipeline" ;
        skos:note "Ends in a check for pricing feedback" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Well, I am just starting to fundraise two things that are happening right now. One, I am looking for more enterprise. Actually it doesn't have to be enterprise. I'm looking for organizations that want to use the thing. Um, the team pricing is about $400 a month. Not about is $400 a month. And then enterprise pricing starts at four grand, plus some setup, plus like, you know, additional consulting fees if they want to do on prem and fancy services and whatnot. First of all, I'm curious if that sounds appropriate to you. One of the things I've been thinking a lot about is the pricing and whether all of that is too low or sort of how the positioning is here. I've been, you know, I'm in a transition period right now where this tool was MCP only for a long time. And I did, you know, all through the spring I was doing beta testing. I had, you know, a couple smaller orgs doing it like I got a ton of feedback and then I got this Enterprise Pilot and like the big feedback coming out of Enterprise Pilot was like, this is fantastic. I don't want to have to do this myself. Can I automatically ingest my teams, meetings and my other services and just have that work? Right. And so, you know, this product is a response to that. Right? Like connect your services and get a feed of all of your calls and just have them like, do the thing. Right." ;
                oa:prefix "ld you like?\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** Yeah.\n\n**" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "23341"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "24688"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

