    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_105 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Strategy feedback: Claude styling, marginal cost of software, telephone company thesis" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "First simple dumb thing. This is dumb. It looks like Claude made the website, which is not wrong, but like everybody's. This is Claude's style is whatever. All Claude does, like, do something different just because, like people look at it and which then leads to my second point. The marginal cost of software development is asymptotically approaching zero. That's not necessarily. That doesn't necessarily mean that there won't be places for people who have more smart to know what needs to be built. Absolutely. Because these machines probably will never be able to infer value generate or they will, but you'll still need to point them directions. One of my operating theses is the telephone company always wins." ;
