    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_109 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Strategy feedback: Moats, disintermediation, and network effects" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "I'll explain. The telephone company always wins because the telephone company sits in between. And it's impossible to disintermediate because they sit in between. Like one of the only durable moats. That's a chatgpt word I think these days is like, is network effects. Right. So because some enterprising person, just like I'm saying I hate slack, I want to build a better slack. Like, we'll be like, I'll make the thing Hollis is having this problem at. Indeed. People are like, I'm just going to make a SaaS version of a thing. Like we pay for the SaaS thing. I'm going to make one right now. Granted, that doesn't, like, doesn't work because they can't use. There's a bunch of reasons why indeed needs to actually pay for a thing that's a real thing. And they don't want to be in the business of building SaaS products. But that's going to change also the moment you become successful. You put a target on your back and so then you're competing with like the graduating class of Stanford and your moat is your first and better, which is an important moat. But like the cost of catch up is slow, is getting cheaper and cheaper and cheaper. So the question is like, how do you become a thing that can't be replaced? How do you become the thing that sits in between? I don't know. But that's like one of my operating theses is like, that's increasingly important." ;
                oa:prefix " context?\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** That is part" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "26244"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "27607"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_110 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_TanyaTeam ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Tanya defends aswritten's moat as the graph of perspective" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "That is part of the thesis here, and maybe I didn't make that clear, is that the real value here is not can I ask questions against my calls, right? Like, that's just rag. As I ingest all of the human decisions over time, it gives me a graph that allows my AIs to work from human decisions instead of unspecified, poorly done documentation or task specs. You talk about AI fucking up, suddenly it truncates at 400 characters or something like that. A lot of those decisions happen in what I think of as like the white space of the prompt, right? If you ask it like, hey, build me a landing page, you get all of these decisions inside the white space or the prompt. And that to me gets filled with organizational perspective, right? And so as much perspective as you can provide, the more your default state is in the direction of your organization. And so like the moat becomes over time, the more calls and decisions that you have ingested into a graph, the graph itself is the moat, right? And like, yes, I'm letting someone store the data in their repo, but the read and manipulation layer is proprietary. And like, yes, they own it, but they can't do very much with it without the platform." ;
                oa:prefix "y important.\n\n**Tanya Team:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Xavier Expert:** Right, ye" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "27625"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "28819"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

    narr:Expr_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720_111 a narr:Expression ;
        narr:actor narr:Actor_XavierExpert ;
        narr:act "assertive" ;
        narr:context "Debating incumbent switching costs and commodification" ;
        oa:hasTarget [ a oa:SpecificResource ;
            oa:hasSource narr:Sample_5RealXavierAndTanya60Mins20260720 ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "Right, yeah, yeah, no, exactly, I see what you're saying. Like, you inside the company, you have a network effect because. And like the process of like, you, you get better as more time goes by and you have more data and your graph gets more robust, et cetera, et cetera. I think that's true and I'm not disagreeing with that. I just think that like, like the, the core problem is like someone comes along and builds a better version of that, right? It's like, okay, the iPhone destroyed TomTom, not because it had better maps, right? Destroyed Garmin, not because it had better maps. Right. Garmin was in everyone's car who wanted to have a car." ;
                oa:prefix "platform.\n\n**Xavier Expert:** " ;
                oa:suffix "\n\n**Tanya Team:** Like a map i" ] ;
            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextPositionSelector ;
                oa:start "28840"^^xsd:integer ;
                oa:end "29486"^^xsd:integer ] ] ;
        prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-23T18:44:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

